simple diode test
* SPICE3 (ngspice-dialect) translation of Gnucap tests/d_diode.6.ckt at gnucap/gnucap@5acb027125d6ea7c546badd03e026d8781c6a400.
* Original: Gnucap regression tests, GPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE-NOTICE.MakeList and COPYING.txt here).
* Modified 2026-10-11 by benchmarks/translate/gnucap-to-spice3.ts (spice-ts issue #524); changes:
*   - commented out `.list` (Gnucap `.list` only echoes the netlist to the console)
*   - commented out `.print op v(1) v(2) i(v1) i(r1) id(d1) vd(d1) req(d1) cap(d1) z(d1) zraw(d1) y(d1) z(2)` (SPICE3 has no `.print op`; the raw file still holds every node voltage and source current)
*   - `.print dc v(1) v(2) i(v1) i(r1) id(d1) vd(d1) req(d1) cap(d1) z(d1) zraw(d1) y(d1) z(2) iter(0)`: Gnucap-only probes i(r1) id(d1) vd(d1) req(d1) cap(d1) z(d1) zraw(d1) y(d1) z(2) iter(0) dropped (no SPICE3 output-variable syntax)
*   - commented out `.stat notime` (Gnucap `.stat` only prints solver statistics)
*   - commented out `.stat notime` (Gnucap `.stat` only prints solver statistics)
* The first line above is the unchanged original title line.
V1   1  0  10.
R1   1  2  100.K
D1   2  0  ddd   m=2. 
.model  ddd  d  ( is= 10.f  rs= 0.  n= 1.  tt= 0.  cjo= 1.p  vj= 1.  m= 0.5 
+ eg= 1.11  xti= 3.  kf= 0.  af= 1.  fc= 0.5 )
*gnucap-only: .list
*gnucap-only: .print op v(1) v(2) i(v1) i(r1) id(d1) vd(d1) req(d1) cap(d1) z(d1) zraw(d1) y(d1) z(2)
.op
.print dc v(1) v(2) i(v1)
.dc v1 -10 10 2
*gnucap-only: .stat notime
.dc v1 9.999 10.001 .001
.op
*gnucap-only: .stat notime
.end
